    "q-48935": {
      "dom_id": "step-q48935",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t)=6\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=4\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2012?$ Round your answer to the nearest integer.",
      "worked_solution": "The rate of change in the crocodile population $t$ years since $2000$ is equal to the birth rate minus the death rate, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2012$ is $12$ years after $2000$, we have $t=12.$ Substituting $t=12,$ the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river  in $2012$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(12)-D(12) & =6\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)}-4\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)} \\\\  & =6{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3} \\\\  & ≈40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river in $2012$ is approximately $40$ crocodiles per year.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
